I think that rec.games.hack.bugs is silly.  The release of 3.0 has
generated a bunch of bug reports.  If you think that these don't
belong in this group you should pressure folks to use
comp.sources.games.bugs.  That is why it exists.

Also, creating rec.games.hack.bugs will take quite some time.  A
minimum of six weeks.  By then the rush of bugs/enhancements will have
probably slowed way done.  The one lonely call for discussion of
rec.games.hack.bugs in news.groups has generated no comment except:
use comp.sources.games.bugs.

Finally, given the newness of 3.0, it is often difficult to
distinguish a bug from a feature.  If you are a player of the game who
is new to 3.0 but with no source how do you tell if monsters picking
up weapons and throwing them isn't a bug?

Well, truly finally, to shut up inews about more included, a flame.
This isn't a `bb'.  It's a USENET news group.  A `bb' to the best of
my knowledge is a small spherical piece of metal shot from an air
rifle.  Newsgroups manage to traverse the world these days. `bb's
mostly manage to mangle mammals.
